// Title: VolumeShadowCopy Symlink Creation Via Mklink
// Sigma ID: 40b19fa6-d835-400c-b301-41f3a2baacaf
// Status: stable | Level: high
// Author: Teymur Kheirkhabarov, oscd.community
// Date: 2019-10-22 | Modified: 2023-03-06
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1003.002, T1003.003
// Description: Shadow Copies storage symbolic link creation using operating systems utilities
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administrator working with shadow copies, access for backup purposes
// References:
//   - https://www.slideshare.net/heirhabarov/hunting-for-credentials-dumping-in-windows-environment
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_cmd_mklink_shadow_copies_access_symlink.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "mklink" and ProcessCommandLine contains "HarddiskVolumeShadowCopy"
